Z||000000||DaveL||06-26-2001||08:43 AM||||Are there any other GM engines that would be plug and play replacement for an 87 2.5 ? Mine died and I'm looking to find a used engine somewhere. Can't afford the $2048 price I was quoted for a GM Target motor, although they offer a 60,000 mile or 3 year warranty, parts and labor.||||reg||5
Z||000001||SteveJ||06-26-2001||09:30 AM||||Literally tons of them. 87 was the first year for this engine which was used for many years in GM cars. Even better the junk yards are now full of them many with very few miles on them at great prices. There have been several threads on this. Put a search on for 87, DIS, maybe 2.5 or anything else you think might pull it up.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011474.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011474.html</A>  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011439.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011439.html</A> <P>links added<p>[This message has been edited by SteveJ (edited 06-26-2001).]||||reg||1
